// DID FISHING STOP, OR WAS IT ALWAYS THIS SLOW? (Corey, 2026-11-24: 27 tuna in 20-30 minutes, where
// the measured cadence and the wiki's own catch rates both say about 14, and other players reporting
// the same for other fish.)
//
// Every rate in fishing has been checked against the wiki and every cadence measured - that is what
// engine/tools/sim/fishingrates.ts holds - so the arithmetic says the build is right and the players
// say it is slow. The one thing neither the sim nor the rates can see is fishing STOPPING partway
// through a trip, because the loop is p_opnpc re-queuing itself every tick and anything that clears
// the player's interaction ends it with no message at all. The player keeps standing there.
//
// So this watches for the stop instead of the rate. Every cast re-arms a ten-tick timer; re-arming
// resets the clock, so while casts keep landing every five or six ticks the timer never fires. It
// can only fire once fishing has stopped, and then it writes down what the state was at that moment.
//
// WHAT IT CANNOT TELL YOU, said plainly: a player who clicked away, walked off or filled their pack
// looks exactly like a player whose interaction was dropped from under them. That is the limit of
// watching from the content side, and it is why the engine logs the other half - Player.ts's
// validateTarget now names every silently dropped interaction. Correlate the two by time: a
// "fishing stopped" here with free space, next to an "interaction dropped silently" there, is the
// bug. A "fishing stopped" with no free space is just a full pack.
// A SOFT TIMER, NOT A NORMAL ONE. A normal timer only runs while the player canAccess(), and a
// filled pack ends fishing with ~mesbox("You can't carry any more fish.") - a modal, which blocks
// normal timers - so the watchdog went blind in exactly the case it most needs to tell apart from a
// silent stop. A soft timer runs either way (Player.processTimers).
[proc,fishing_watchdog_arm]
%fishing_last_cast = map_clock;
softtimer(fishing_watchdog, ^fishing_watchdog_ticks);

[softtimer,fishing_watchdog]
def_int $since = calc(map_clock - %fishing_last_cast);
if ($since < ^fishing_watchdog_ticks) {
    return;
}
clearsofttimer(fishing_watchdog);
%fishing_last_cast = 0;
def_int $space = inv_freespace(inv);
session_log(^log_adventure, "Fishing stopped: no cast for <tostring($since)> ticks, <tostring($space)> free slots");
// STAFF ONLY, and deliberately not a player-facing message. Making it one would be a change to how
// the game reads rather than a way to find out why it reads that way - and if the answer turns out
// to be that fishing is being dropped, the fix belongs where the dropping happens, not in a notice
// that it happened.
if (staffmodlevel > 0) {
    mes("@dre@[fishing] stopped after <tostring($since)> ticks with <tostring($space)> free slots.");
}
